    "interpretation": "OOB bootstraps rows, not genomes. Rows from the same genome land both in-bag and out-of-bag, so an OOB estimate is scored against near-neighbours from the same annotation run. The gap between OOB and the genome-grouped CV mean is therefore a measurement of genome-level leakage, not a discrepancy to be explained away. OOB above grouped CV is the expected direction and its size is the quantity of interest."
