    "gap": 0.04698,
    "interpretation": "The gap is a measurement of genome-level leakage. OOB resamples rows, so a held-out row is scored by trees that saw its neighbours from the same genome and the same annotation run. Grouped CV holds whole genomes out. The difference is what that leakage is worth, not an error in either estimate."
  }
